# Binned legends: guide_bins

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`guide_bins()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/guide_bins.html), in the order the page
gives them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and then Giggly's. An example Giggly cannot
draw yet keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is waiting for, so the page is also a list of
what remains.

`guide_bins()` is the legend of a binned scale: a version of `guide_legend()` that puts its ticks
between the keys, at the bins' edges, and draws a small axis to show the binning. It serves any
aesthetic but position, though colour and fill default to `guide_coloursteps()`, and it merges
aesthetics mapped the same way into one legend. Giggly has none of it yet: it has no binned scales,
and draws a legend for each of alpha, colour and fill and a colour bar for a continuous colour or
fill, none of them binned.

## The standard look

```r
p <- ggplot(mtcars) +
  geom_point(aes(disp, mpg, size = hp)) +
  scale_size_binned()

# Standard look
p
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size`, the binned scale that maps it, `scale_size_binned()`, and the
legend that reads it back, `guide_bins()`.

## Removing the legend's axis

```r
# Remove the axis or style it
p + guides(size = guide_bins(
  theme = theme(legend.axis.line = element_blank())
))
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size`, `scale_size_binned()`, `guide_bins()`, and changing the theme,
here to remove the legend's axis line.

## Showing the limits

```r
p + guides(size = guide_bins(show.limits = TRUE))
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size`, `scale_size_binned()`, and `guide_bins()` with its `show.limits`
option, which labels the ends of the scale too.

## Arrows on the legend's axis

R's `arrow()` describes arrowheads, here 1.5 mm long, at both ends of a line.

```r
my_arrow <- arrow(length = unit(1.5, "mm"), ends = "both")
p + guides(size = guide_bins(
  theme = theme(legend.axis.line = element_line(arrow = my_arrow))
))
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size`, `scale_size_binned()`, `guide_bins()`, and changing the theme,
here to put arrowheads on the legend's axis line.

## Merged legends

Mapping `size` and `colour` to the same column, each through a binned scale, gives one legend for
both.

```r
# Guides are merged together if possible
ggplot(mtcars) +
  geom_point(aes(disp, mpg, size = hp, colour = hp)) +
  scale_size_binned() +
  scale_colour_binned(guide = "bins")
```

Not in Giggly yet: mapping `size`, `scale_size_binned()`, `scale_colour_binned()`, and
`guide_bins()`, which merges the two into one legend.